{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having a burning pain in your chest and upper belly for the past few days?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s been really bad—like a fire moving up from my stomach into my throat. It feels just like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you didn’t stop your tube feeds before coming in?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I kept them going. I only drank water by mouth. I didn’t want to make things worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ve reviewed your history. You’ve had this kind of pain before, linked to reflux and ulcers after your gastric bypass reversal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right. Last time, changing the feeding formula and starting erythromycin helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ve started you on an IV medication—pantoprazole—to reduce stomach acid and protect your esophagus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Is it safe to keep my tube feeds going?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re continuing them. We’re also increasing the rate a bit because your nutrition needs are high. We want to avoid another drop in your blood sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been worried about that too. The hypoglycemia scares me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring it closely. Your erythromycin is still running—it helps your stomach empty better, which should help with both reflux and sugar control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the cholestyramine? I’ve never taken that before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It binds bile acids that can worsen reflux. It’s often helpful in cases like yours. We’ll give it twice a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try it. Should I be worried about the pain getting worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching closely. We did an X-ray earlier—no blockage or free air. Your bowels look normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Do you think it’s another ulcer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible. The GI team wants to do an EGD—upper endoscopy—to check your stomach and the surgical connections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When will that happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow morning. We’ll keep you comfortable until then. We also added prochlorperazine for nausea if it flares up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-08-01 15:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I just want this burning to stop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-08-02 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You did well during the EGD this morning. I have the results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-08-02 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How did it go? Did you see what’s causing the pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-08-02 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. There’s inflammation in your stomach—gastritis—and some small, healing ulcers near the surgical connection where your stomach meets the tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-08-02 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not bleeding or perforated?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-08-02 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, the ulcers are clean-based, which means they’re not actively bleeding. There’s also a slight narrowing in your stomach anatomy that may be slowing emptying and contributing to reflux."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-08-02 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s why the burning keeps coming back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-08-02 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The GI team recommends staying on the pantoprazole, but now twice a day instead of once. We’ll also keep the sucralfate to coat the ulcers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-08-02 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the erythromycin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-08-02 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re continuing it. It helps move things through. We’re also adding ranitidine at bedtime—it gives extra acid control overnight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-08-02 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Can I try eating anything by mouth now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-08-02 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with small sips and soft foods. Your stomach needs time to heal. If you tolerate it, we’ll gradually increase."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-08-03 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Your pain is much better, and you’ve kept down your oral intake."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-08-03 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the burning is mostly gone. I had some applesauce and broth yesterday with no problems."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-08-03 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’re going to reduce your tube feeds back to your home rate since you’re eating more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-08-03 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I prefer to eat normally when I can."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-08-03 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep supporting you. Your labs are stable—no anemia worsening, and your electrolytes are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-08-04 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made steady progress. Pain is controlled, you’re tolerating a full stage 3 diet, and your bowel function is normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-08-04 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-08-04 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for discharge on Friday. We’ll make sure you have all your medications sorted."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-08-04 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need new prescriptions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-08-04 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ll take pantoprazole twice daily now, cholestyramine twice a day, and ranitidine at night. All your other meds stay the same."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-08-04 14:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the tube feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-08-04 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Back to your usual schedule—continuous overnight and bolus during the day as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-08-05 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your follow-up is set with Dr. Kim next week. They’ll monitor your ulcer healing and reflux."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-08-05 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. Should I sleep upright?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-08-05 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, elevate the head of your bed. It helps reduce nighttime reflux. Also avoid lying down right after eating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-08-06 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check: you’re pain-free, eating well, and labs are stable. Discharge is tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-08-06 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m so glad. Thank you for helping me feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-08-06 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember: call if the pain returns, or if you vomit blood, run a fever, or can’t keep fluids down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-08-06 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll keep taking all the meds as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2174-08-07 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home. Your tube site looks great—no redness or drainage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2174-08-07 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel so much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2174-08-07 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the goal. Keep resting, stay upright after meals, and follow up with Dr. Kim."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2174-08-07 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. Thank you again, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2174-08-07 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re here if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-08-01 15:05:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-08-07 18:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with a three-day history of epigastric and esophageal burning pain, similar to prior episodes linked to gastrojejunal ulcers and reflux. She remained on tube feeds throughout and was started on IV pantoprazole, cholestyramine, and continued erythromycin for gastric motility. An EGD revealed clean-based ulcers at the gastro-gastric anastomosis, gastric friability, and antral erythema consistent with gastritis. Her symptoms improved with increased acid suppression using pantoprazole twice daily, addition of ranitidine, and continuation of sucralfate. Oral intake was advanced successfully, tube feeds were reduced to baseline, and she was discharged home with medication adjustments and a follow-up appointment. She remained hemodynamically stable throughout, with no complications.",
    "problems": [
      "Esophagitis, unspecified",
      "Gastritis, unspecified, without bleeding",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Functional dyspepsia",
      "Gastrojejunal ulcer, unspecified as acute or chronic, without hemorrhage or perforation",
      "Gastrostomy status"
    ]
  }
}
